  "subRow": "Battalion on extended frontages, two companies and three platoons up",
  "note": "As IBB Annex U App 7 (p 482 by the contents; the page is unnumbered, PDF 499) draws it: a Bn on extended frontages, 6300 m, with two Coys up, each with its three Pls up in a row (Pl localities 600 m, IBB Annex U App 5 p 480; 300 m between the Pls, 800 m between the Coys: 5600 m held, 350 m flanks inside the 6300 m, calc), the Pl localities 500 m deep (the annex's 500 m), and two Coys in depth, one behind each forward Coy; depth 3000-4000 m (laid at 3050 m, the short end, for the reserve's reach, E). Larger gaps only where a Bde reserve can close them (IBB S59 p 327); a Coy's own frontage is never extended (S59 para 6 b p 326): the Pls keep their 600 m, only the intervals open. Bn HQ (IBB S3 pp 22-24; p 23: placed centrally within the Bn locality, preferably behind the depth localities; a defended locality of 55 all ranks, concealed from the air, dug in, near the Bde axis with an alternative posn; laid about 500 m behind the depth Coys, between them (the distance a decision, E). The RRs, a section of two in each rifle Coy, sited first in the forward localities with an alternative each 200-300 m back (IBB S8 pp 38-42; IC p 367). Books differ: the forward Coys here hold no Pl in depth (IBB App 7); IC s84 para 7 c p 447 says depth at Coy and Bn level must always be retained, and para 11 p 448 gives its frontage options in Annex R, which Material/IC.pdf does not hold (no annex pages): IBB's drawing is kept, depth held by the two depth Coys. Protective minefield (PlanObstacles, the user's trace of 28 Nov 2026): panels round the front of each forward Coy and its open flank, about 200 m out (IC s111 para 5 p 651), up to 250 m deep (IC s107 p 596), patrol lanes between them (IC s74 para 18 a p 394); the depth Coys' open flanks closed to contain a penetration (none beside the reserve: its way out kept clear) (IC s74 para 19 c p 395), their rear left open for the counter-attack. A screen 1 km ahead of the FDLs (AMP p 1.2) by a Pl of C Coy (IBB S54 para 4 c pp 284-285: its troops from the depth Coys).",
